WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:13.490
Part five: alcohol spots. This part is optional, only if you want to work alcohol spots. It's for adults only, and you need both the training and a permit before your first alcohol shift.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:20.698
Step one: alcohol server training. On your paperwork page, open the Alcohol server training card.

00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:30.072
Take ATC Server Training on the Indiana ATC site, under the Education tab. There's a how-to guide right there. It's good for three years.

00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:31.873
Pick which training you took.

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:35.721
Your certificate should look like this, with your name and the date.

00:00:35.921 --> 00:00:40.650
Enter the date you completed it, upload the certificate, and tap Submit.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:56.541
Step two: the ATC volunteer permit. Apply on the Indiana ATC site. If you're twenty-one or older, it's the Volunteer Employee Permit. Eighteen to twenty is a restricted permit, cashier only. It's good for two years.

00:00:56.741 --> 00:01:07.493
Your permit comes by email, and not right away. The ATC reviews your application first, which can take a few days. The application or payment receipt isn't the permit.

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:11.022
When it comes, upload the full page, or the wallet card.

00:01:11.222 --> 00:01:18.080
Enter the permit number, which starts with VB, and the expiration date, then upload it and tap Submit.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:25.620
Your volunteer page reminds you that the permit comes by email. Upload it as soon as it arrives.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:37.150
That's the whole series! Find a shift by tapping Open spots on your volunteer page. Questions? Email the IU liaison from the bottom of any Hub page.
